  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend part PP of chapter 58 of the laws of 2020 amending the\nenvironmental conservation law relating to expanded polystyrene foam container\nand polystyrene loose fill packaging ban, and amending the state finance law\nrelating to moneys collected for violations of the expanded polystyrene foam\ncontainer and polystyrene loose fill packaging ban, in relation to extending\nthe effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S9767",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9767-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Part PP §4, Chap 58 of 2020",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9767\n\nSPONSOR: KRUEGER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend part PP of chapter 58 of the laws of 2020 amending the\nenvironmental conservation law relating to expanded polystyrene foam\ncontainer and polystyrene loose fill packaging ban, and amending the\nstate finance law relating to moneys collected for violations of the\nexpanded polystyrene foam container and polystyrene loose fill packaging\nban, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend the ability for counties to retain\nfees relating to the enforcement of the polystyrene container and loose\nfill ban.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill would extend, for five years, until January 1,\n2030, the ability for counties to retain any fines collected by a\nproceeding to enforce the polystyrene packaging foam container and loose\nfill ban which was initiated by the county.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe polystyrene foam container and loose fill ban, enacted in 2010, has\nhelped reduce the amount of waste and litter in New York and improved\nthe recyclability of packing materials overall. This bill is necessary\nto ensure that counties retain an incentive to help with enforcement of\nthis act.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
